## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical design of a CKNE-aware serverless scheduler that balances latency guarantees with multi-tenant fairness under dynamic CKNE scoring.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-driven per-tenant concurrency budgets and burst allowances
- Warm/cold-start pool management with eviction semantics
- Minute-by-minute degradation loop and capacity reallocation logic
- Comprehensive telemetry, SLA verification, and preemption rules

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo quota calculator
function quotaForTenant(ckne, base) {
  const soft = Math.max(1, Math.floor(base * ckne));
  const burst = Math.floor(soft * (1 + ckne));
  const coldPool = Math.ceil(ckne * 10);
  return { soft, burst, coldPool };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Real-world BI workloads multiplex dozens to thousands of tenants; CKNE-driven concurrency and memory control is critical for SLOs and fair sharing.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-resource mapping: concurrency, memory budget, spill/IO throttling
- Per-tenant quotas and dynamic reallocation cadence
- Fairness guarantees and explicit preemption rules
- Telemetry hooks and feedback for regret-free adjustment

## Code Example
```javascript
function allocate(tenants){
  // normalize CKNE 0-1 to weight, compute quotas
  const total = tenants.reduce((a,t)=>a+t.ckne,0);
  tenants.forEach(t=>{ t.alloc = t.ckne/total; });
  return tenants;
}
```

